---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 41,
    title: "Finite State Fun",
    description: "Drive title, play, and game-over screens with clean state logic.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 42,
    title: "Random Opponents",
    description: "Blend patrol and chase behaviours with weighted randomness.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 43,
    title: "Shooting Stars",
    description: "Launch, recycle, and pace projectiles with cooldowns.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 44,
    title: "Hit Detection",
    description: "React to sprite collisions with flashes, score bumps, and respawns.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 45,
    title: "Power-Ups",
    description: "Spawn buffs, trigger effects, and cleanly expire them.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 46,
    title: "Balancing Act",
    description: "Ramp speed and spawn timers without overwhelming the player.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 47,
    title: "Saving Scores",
    description: "Keep a high-score table in arrays and write it to disk.",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 48,
    title: "Cosmic Clash",
    description: "Mini-game weaving states, AI, power-ups, and persistence together.",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout title="Week 6: Game Logic - Commodore 64">
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4f46e5 0%, #7c3aed 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .course-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .stat-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #4f46e5;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #4f46e5;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .intro-section p,
    .intro-section ul {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .intro-section ul {
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }

    .intro-section li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #4f46e5;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.12);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4f46e5 0%, #7c3aed 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.1);
      color: #4f46e5;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #4f46e5 0%, #7c3aed 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(79, 70, 229, 0.3);
    }
  </style>

  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">WEEK 6: GAME LOGIC</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">States, AI bursts, projectiles, power-ups, Cosmic Clash</p>

    <p class="course-description">
      Week 6 turns moving sprites into living systems. You’ll organise your program with finite states, give enemies
      personality with weighted randomness, let the player fire back, recognise collisions instantly, sprinkle in
      power-ups, and pace difficulty so tension builds. Everything funnels into the **Cosmic Clash** mini-game—a survival
      shooter that records high scores.
    </p>

    <div class="course-stats">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">8</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Systems Lessons</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">1</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Mini-Game</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">3</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Saveable Scores</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="content-container">
    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You’ll Build This Week</h2>
      <p>
        Week 5 stretched the map; Week 6 makes it feel alive. Each lesson layers a new piece of game logic so your worlds
        react, surprise, reward, and escalate:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Lesson 41:</strong> Use a tidy state machine to swap between title, play, and game-over screens.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 42:</strong> Give drones patrol and chase moods with randomness that still feels fair.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 43:</strong> Launch reusable projectiles that obey cooldowns and fly independently.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 44:</strong> React to sprite collisions instantly—flash colours, award points, respawn.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 45:</strong> Spawn buffs, power the player up, and time their expiration.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 46:</strong> Balance speed and spawn rates so difficulty climbs without becoming cruel.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 47:</strong> Maintain and save a high-score table just like the arcades did.</li>
        <li><strong>Lesson 48:</strong> Ship <em>Cosmic Clash</em>, weaving every system into a replayable mini-game.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        By the end of the week you’ll have a state-driven shooter that reacts to the player, rewards mastery, and even
        remembers their initials for next time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>
      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/commodore-64/basic/week-6/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(2, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Command the Chaos?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        These eight lessons turn mechanics into systems. Build smarter enemies, responsive weapons, meaningful rewards,
        and a mini-game that feels alive.
      </p>
      <a href="/commodore-64/basic/week-6/lesson-41" class="start-button">Start Lesson 41: Finite State Fun</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
